Subject: [PATCH] The save in the lower menu's panel (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With the lower menu on and the Pokétch up, SAVE ends the Pokétch behind
the panel's black and draws a save page on the sub engine, tall: the
message box at the top, a report card (the trainer's picture, the name,
IDNo., the place, POKéDEX, TIME, the badges at half size, the party's
icons) and YES / NO buttons the port takes touches on. The save's own
script runs unchanged: while the page is up its message box opens on
the page, its YES/NO is the page's buttons, and the save info window
isn't shown. When the script ends the panel fades to black and the
Pokétch starts again. Without the menu it's the DS's save.
